[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [{:db/id 17592186078558 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-f438fee9-fd2e-5bc4-8ed6-aceb6e4fcc33" "question-91775cc6-b3ff-5403-8a6d-5a5294e1af4c"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186078202 :question/problem "The first term of a geometric sequence is $2$, and the common ratio is $3.$ What is the $9$th term?" :question/worked-solution "The first term is $a_1=2,$ and the common ratio is $r=3,$ so we can write the formula for the $n$th term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {r}^{n-1} \\\\  & =2\\cdot {3}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the $9$th term, we can use this formula with $n={\\color{blue}9}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =2\\cdot {3}^{n-1} \\\\ {a}_{9} & =2\\cdot {3}^{9-1} \\\\  & =2\\cdot {3}^{8} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 6561 \\\\  & =13\\,122\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $9$th term is $a_{9}=13\\,122.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186078559 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-1bbae00a-a76f-5b1d-a767-0acf7498bde8" "question-18bc1e21-0c4b-52f3-824f-e719cd86e034"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186078204 :question/problem "Find the formula for the $n$th term of a sequence if the $6$th term is $80$ and the common ratio is $-2.$" :question/worked-solution "The common ratio is $r=-2,$ so we can start writing the formula for the $n$th term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {r}^{n-1} \\\\  & ={a}_{1}\\cdot (-2)^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, we still need to figure out the first term $a_1.$ We know that the $6$th term is $a_6=80,$ so we can solve for the first term as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{6} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot (-2)^{6-1} \\\\ 80 & ={a}_{1}\\cdot (-2)^{5} \\\\ 80 & ={a}_{1}\\cdot (-32) \\\\ -\\frac{80}{32} & ={a}_{1} \\\\ -\\frac{5}{2} & ={a}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that we know the first term is $a_1=-\\dfrac{5}{2},$ we can complete the formula for the $n$th term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot (-2)^{n-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{2}\\cdot (-2)^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can simplify a bit further by manipulating the exponents, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =-\\frac{5}{2}(-2)^{n-1} \\\\  & =5\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2})\\cdot (-2)^{n-1} \\\\  & =5\\cdot (-2)^{-1}\\cdot (-2)^{n-1} \\\\  & =5\\cdot (-2)^{n-2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186078560 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-cb4d13f6-05f0-58f1-8216-e5e0e82521cb" "question-b5f78cff-3c2d-5ff5-b715-c8fb25e53460"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186078203 :question/problem "Given that the $5$th term of a geometric sequence is $9$, and the common ratio is $3,$ find the second term." :question/worked-solution "The common ratio is $r=3,$ so we can start writing the formula for the $n$th term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {r}^{n-1} \\\\  & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {3}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, we still need to figure out the first term $a_1.$ We know that the $5$th term is $a_5=9,$ so we can solve for the first term as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{5} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {3}^{5-1} \\\\ 9 & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {3}^{4} \\\\ 9 & ={a}_{1}\\cdot 81 \\\\ \\frac{9}{81} & ={a}_{1} \\\\ \\frac{1}{9} & ={a}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that we know the first term is $a_1=\\dfrac{1}{9},$ we can complete the formula for the $n$th term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {3}^{n-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\cdot {3}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we can use this formula to compute the second term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{9}\\cdot {3}^{2-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the second term is $a_2 = \\dfrac{1}{3}.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-f438fee9-fd2e-5bc4-8ed6-aceb6e4fcc33" :question/id #uuid "f438fee9-fd2e-5bc4-8ed6-aceb6e4fcc33" :question/math-academy-id "q-265738" :question/problem "The first term of a geometric sequence is $32,$ and the common ratio is $-\\frac{1}{2}.$  The $12$th term of this sequence is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The first term is ${a}_{1}=32,$ and the common ratio is $r=-\\frac{1}{2},$ so we can write the formula for the $n$th term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {r}^{n-1} \\\\  & =32\\cdot {(-\\frac{1}{2})}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the $12$th term, we can use this formula with $n=12:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =32\\cdot {(-\\frac{1}{2})}^{n-1} \\\\ {a}_{12} & =32\\cdot {(-\\frac{1}{2})}^{12-1} \\\\  & =32\\cdot {(-\\frac{1}{2})}^{11} \\\\  & =-{2}^{5}\\cdot \\frac{1}{{2}^{11}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{2}^{6}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{64}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $12$th term is ${a}_{12}=-\\frac{1}{64}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-26653816-dfb8-59e5-8d87-31577cdbb120"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-26653816-dfb8-59e5-8d87-31577cdbb120" :answer-field/id #uuid "26653816-dfb8-59e5-8d87-31577cdbb120" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-1dd5ec84-7a08-5f98-8682-c2c50317fdda" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1dd5ec84-7a08-5f98-8682-c2c50317fdda"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1dd5ec84-7a08-5f98-8682-c2c50317fdda" :answer/id #uuid "1dd5ec84-7a08-5f98-8682-c2c50317fdda" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{64}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-91775cc6-b3ff-5403-8a6d-5a5294e1af4c" :question/id #uuid "91775cc6-b3ff-5403-8a6d-5a5294e1af4c" :question/math-academy-id "q-265737" :question/problem "The first term of a geometric sequence is $-\\frac{1}{81},$ and the common ratio is $-3.$ The $9$th term of this sequence is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The first term is ${a}_{1}=-\\frac{1}{81},$ and the common ratio is $r=-3,$ so we can write the formula for the $n$th term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {r}^{n-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{81}\\cdot (-3)^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the $9$th term, we can use this formula with $n=9:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =-\\frac{1}{81}\\cdot (-3)^{n-1} \\\\ {a}_{9} & =-\\frac{1}{81}\\cdot (-3)^{9-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{81}\\cdot (-3)^{8} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{3}^{4}}\\cdot {3}^{8} \\\\  & =-{3}^{4} \\\\  & =-81\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $9$th term is ${a}_{9}=-81.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b77092c7-1268-5f33-a5db-81532ae19c78"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b77092c7-1268-5f33-a5db-81532ae19c78" :answer-field/id #uuid "b77092c7-1268-5f33-a5db-81532ae19c78" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-910334bb-a236-530a-b15b-4e9e5b6ad92e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-910334bb-a236-530a-b15b-4e9e5b6ad92e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-910334bb-a236-530a-b15b-4e9e5b6ad92e" :answer/id #uuid "910334bb-a236-530a-b15b-4e9e5b6ad92e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-81" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-1bbae00a-a76f-5b1d-a767-0acf7498bde8" :question/id #uuid "1bbae00a-a76f-5b1d-a767-0acf7498bde8" :question/math-academy-id "q-5449" :question/problem "Find the equation for the $n$th term of a geometric sequence if the $5$th term is $16$ and the common ratio is $\\frac{2}{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "The common ratio is $r=\\frac{2}{3},$ so we can start writing the formula for the $n$th term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {r}^{n-1} \\\\  & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {(\\frac{2}{3})}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, we still need to figure out the first term ${a}_{1}.$ We know that the $5$th term is ${a}_{5}=16,$ so we can solve for the first term as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{5} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {(\\frac{2}{3})}^{5-1} \\\\ 16 & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {(\\frac{2}{3})}^{4} \\\\ {2}^{4} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot (\\frac{{2}^{4}}{{3}^{4}}) \\\\ \\frac{{2}^{4}\\cdot {3}^{4}}{{2}^{4}} & ={a}_{1} \\\\ {3}^{4} & ={a}_{1} \\\\ 81 & ={a}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that we know the first term is ${a}_{1}=81,$ we can complete the formula for the $n$th term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {(\\frac{2}{3})}^{n-1} \\\\  & =81\\cdot {(\\frac{2}{3})}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-93f0a508-6eba-52dd-97c6-cb5ace58658c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-93f0a508-6eba-52dd-97c6-cb5ace58658c" :answer-field/id #uuid "93f0a508-6eba-52dd-97c6-cb5ace58658c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-eca10867-76a4-52f1-be58-955b24419718" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0aa368f5-9980-5af5-a908-3b9b819b0121" "answer-a7cb3144-a22f-5f9b-a7a4-6681a52052c2" "answer-a8bc2a3c-15ca-50bd-b78f-91ffcfb5a2d5" "answer-cc516a3f-e478-5de4-865d-84d26bdbc656" "answer-eca10867-76a4-52f1-be58-955b24419718"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0aa368f5-9980-5af5-a908-3b9b819b0121" :answer/id #uuid "0aa368f5-9980-5af5-a908-3b9b819b0121" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n}=100\\cdot {(\\frac{2}{3})}^{n-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a7cb3144-a22f-5f9b-a7a4-6681a52052c2" :answer/id #uuid "a7cb3144-a22f-5f9b-a7a4-6681a52052c2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n}=16\\cdot {(\\frac{2}{3})}^{n-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a8bc2a3c-15ca-50bd-b78f-91ffcfb5a2d5" :answer/id #uuid "a8bc2a3c-15ca-50bd-b78f-91ffcfb5a2d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n}=49\\cdot {(\\frac{2}{3})}^{n-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cc516a3f-e478-5de4-865d-84d26bdbc656" :answer/id #uuid "cc516a3f-e478-5de4-865d-84d26bdbc656" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n}=64\\cdot {(\\frac{2}{3})}^{n-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eca10867-76a4-52f1-be58-955b24419718" :answer/id #uuid "eca10867-76a4-52f1-be58-955b24419718" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n}=81\\cdot {(\\frac{2}{3})}^{n-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-18bc1e21-0c4b-52f3-824f-e719cd86e034" :question/id #uuid "18bc1e21-0c4b-52f3-824f-e719cd86e034" :question/math-academy-id "q-5450" :question/problem "Find the equation for the $n$th term of a geometric sequence if the $6$th term is $-\\frac{1}{5}$ and the common ratio is $-\\frac{1}{5}.$" :question/worked-solution "The common ratio is $r=-\\frac{1}{5},$ so we can start writing the formula for the $n$th term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {r}^{n-1} \\\\  & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {(-\\frac{1}{5})}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, we still need to figure out the first term ${a}_{1}.$ We know that the $6$th term is ${a}_{6}=-\\frac{1}{5},$ so we can solve for the first term as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{6} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {(-\\frac{1}{5})}^{6-1} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{5} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {(-\\frac{1}{5})}^{5} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{5} & =-{a}_{1}\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{5})}^{5} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{5} & =-{a}_{1}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{{5}^{5}}) \\\\ {5}^{4} & ={a}_{1} \\\\ 625 & ={a}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that we know the first term is ${a}_{1}=625,$ we can complete the formula for the $n$th term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {(-\\frac{1}{5})}^{n-1} \\\\  & =625\\cdot {(-\\frac{1}{5})}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9d6e6324-1bb7-5c0e-a897-1048511dc113"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9d6e6324-1bb7-5c0e-a897-1048511dc113" :answer-field/id #uuid "9d6e6324-1bb7-5c0e-a897-1048511dc113" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-838f58f2-22d1-5628-b984-cb6bd81d4f74" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7d26afe6-a3f8-5d84-83c8-1468c5a521e7" "answer-f723a1bb-4bd1-5093-8a09-931299bce976" "answer-d08576a1-0a16-5570-9a0f-9b630cd00e74" "answer-0b365dcf-dfb8-5ede-acf7-bff7804315f6" "answer-838f58f2-22d1-5628-b984-cb6bd81d4f74"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7d26afe6-a3f8-5d84-83c8-1468c5a521e7" :answer/id #uuid "7d26afe6-a3f8-5d84-83c8-1468c5a521e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n}=-125\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{5})}^{n-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f723a1bb-4bd1-5093-8a09-931299bce976" :answer/id #uuid "f723a1bb-4bd1-5093-8a09-931299bce976" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n}=-625\\cdot {(-\\frac{1}{5})}^{n-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d08576a1-0a16-5570-9a0f-9b630cd00e74" :answer/id #uuid "d08576a1-0a16-5570-9a0f-9b630cd00e74" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n}=-625\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{5})}^{n}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0b365dcf-dfb8-5ede-acf7-bff7804315f6" :answer/id #uuid "0b365dcf-dfb8-5ede-acf7-bff7804315f6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n}=125\\cdot {(-\\frac{1}{5})}^{n}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-838f58f2-22d1-5628-b984-cb6bd81d4f74" :answer/id #uuid "838f58f2-22d1-5628-b984-cb6bd81d4f74" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n}=625\\cdot {(-\\frac{1}{5})}^{n-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-cb4d13f6-05f0-58f1-8216-e5e0e82521cb" :question/id #uuid "cb4d13f6-05f0-58f1-8216-e5e0e82521cb" :question/math-academy-id "q-265843" :question/problem "If the sixth term of a geometric sequence is $\\frac{1}{16}$ and the common ratio is $\\frac{1}{4},$ then the third term of this sequence is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The common ratio is $r=\\frac{1}{4},$ so we can start writing the formula for the $n$th term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {r}^{n-1} \\\\  & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{4})}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, we still need to figure out the first term ${a}_{1}.$ We know that the $6$th term is ${a}_{6}=16,$ so we can solve for the first term as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{6} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{4})}^{6-1} \\\\ \\frac{1}{16} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{4})}^{5} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{4}^{2}} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot \\frac{1}{{4}^{5}} \\\\ \\frac{{4}^{5}}{{4}^{2}} & ={a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =64\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that we know the first term is ${a}_{1}=64,$ we can complete the formula for the $n$th term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{4})}^{n-1} \\\\  & =64\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{4})}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we can use this formula to compute the third term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{3} & =64\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{4})}^{3-1} \\\\  & ={4}^{3}\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{4})}^{2} \\\\  & ={4}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{{4}^{2}} \\\\  & ={4}^{1} \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the third term  is ${a}_{3}=4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-821f6ff9-8b02-5321-9f6c-8231f646103b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-821f6ff9-8b02-5321-9f6c-8231f646103b" :answer-field/id #uuid "821f6ff9-8b02-5321-9f6c-8231f646103b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-f7fc47b7-94cb-597e-9fb8-34e73e5166b1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f7fc47b7-94cb-597e-9fb8-34e73e5166b1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f7fc47b7-94cb-597e-9fb8-34e73e5166b1" :answer/id #uuid "f7fc47b7-94cb-597e-9fb8-34e73e5166b1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-b5f78cff-3c2d-5ff5-b715-c8fb25e53460" :question/id #uuid "b5f78cff-3c2d-5ff5-b715-c8fb25e53460" :question/math-academy-id "q-109828" :question/problem "Given that the $5$th term of a geometric sequence is $-125$, and the common ratio is $5,$ find the formula for the $n$th term." :question/worked-solution "The common ratio is $r=5,$ so we can start writing the formula for the $n$th term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {r}^{n-1} \\\\  & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {5}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, we still need to figure out the first term ${a}_{1}.$ We know that the $5$th term is ${a}_{5}=-125,$ so we can solve for the first term as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{5} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {5}^{5-1} \\\\ -125 & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {5}^{4} \\\\ -{5}^{3} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {5}^{4} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{5} & ={a}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that we know the first term is ${a}_{1}=-\\frac{1}{5},$ we can complete the formula for the $n$th term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {5}^{n-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot {5}^{n-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{{5}^{n-1}}{5} \\\\  & =-{5}^{n-2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0d82d16e-44b2-54a6-8e45-2ab848923d07"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0d82d16e-44b2-54a6-8e45-2ab848923d07" :answer-field/id #uuid "0d82d16e-44b2-54a6-8e45-2ab848923d07" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-fce13607-7057-5951-b22c-0a53487566f8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1d9acfbd-b37d-5bf8-8563-021375b3f0ac" "answer-71563d96-72fd-5a7a-873a-b97ad8340ba8" "answer-eec28517-10af-546d-b87d-a5fb95584b92" "answer-0a702943-5d20-5d78-b4eb-5b9620b8469b" "answer-fce13607-7057-5951-b22c-0a53487566f8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1d9acfbd-b37d-5bf8-8563-021375b3f0ac" :answer/id #uuid "1d9acfbd-b37d-5bf8-8563-021375b3f0ac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n}=-(-5)^{n-2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-71563d96-72fd-5a7a-873a-b97ad8340ba8" :answer/id #uuid "71563d96-72fd-5a7a-873a-b97ad8340ba8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n}=-{(\\frac{1}{5})}^{n-2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eec28517-10af-546d-b87d-a5fb95584b92" :answer/id #uuid "eec28517-10af-546d-b87d-a5fb95584b92" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n}=-{(\\frac{1}{5})}^{n}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0a702943-5d20-5d78-b4eb-5b9620b8469b" :answer/id #uuid "0a702943-5d20-5d78-b4eb-5b9620b8469b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n}=-{5}^{n-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fce13607-7057-5951-b22c-0a53487566f8" :answer/id #uuid "fce13607-7057-5951-b22c-0a53487566f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n}=-{5}^{n-2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186079626 :tutorial/content "The general formula for the $n$th term of a geometric sequence is \n\n$$\na_n = a_1 \\cdot r^{n-1},\n$$\n\nwhere $a_1$ is the first term and $r$ is the common ratio.\n\nTo illustrate how this works, suppose we want to find the $10$th term of the following geometric sequence:\n\n$$\n3, \\: 6, \\: 12, \\: \\ldots\n$$\n\nThe first term is $a_1=3,$ and the common ratio is $r=2,$ so we can write the formula for the $n$th term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {r}^{n-1} \\\\  & =3\\cdot {2}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the $10$th term, we can use this formula with $n={\\color{blue}10}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =3\\cdot {2}^{n-1} \\\\ {a}_{10} & =3\\cdot {2}^{10-1} \\\\  & =3\\cdot {2}^{9} \\\\  & =3\\cdot 512 \\\\  & =1\\,536\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $10$th term is $a_{10}=1\\,536.$ Using the formula was much quicker than writing out all $10$ terms of the sequence!" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186078695 :activity/expected-seconds 600.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}] "assertions" [[17592186078202 :question/problem "The first term of a geometric sequence is $2$, and the common ratio is $3.$ What is the $9$th term?"] [17592186078202 :question/worked-solution "The first term is $a_1=2,$ and the common ratio is $r=3,$ so we can write the formula for the $n$th term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {r}^{n-1} \\\\  & =2\\cdot {3}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the $9$th term, we can use this formula with $n={\\color{blue}9}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =2\\cdot {3}^{n-1} \\\\ {a}_{9} & =2\\cdot {3}^{9-1} \\\\  & =2\\cdot {3}^{8} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 6561 \\\\  & =13\\,122\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $9$th term is $a_{9}=13\\,122.$"] [17592186078204 :question/problem "Find the formula for the $n$th term of a sequence if the $6$th term is $80$ and the common ratio is $-2.$"] [17592186078204 :question/worked-solution "The common ratio is $r=-2,$ so we can start writing the formula for the $n$th term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {r}^{n-1} \\\\  & ={a}_{1}\\cdot (-2)^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, we still need to figure out the first term $a_1.$ We know that the $6$th term is $a_6=80,$ so we can solve for the first term as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{6} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot (-2)^{6-1} \\\\ 80 & ={a}_{1}\\cdot (-2)^{5} \\\\ 80 & ={a}_{1}\\cdot (-32) \\\\ -\\frac{80}{32} & ={a}_{1} \\\\ -\\frac{5}{2} & ={a}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that we know the first term is $a_1=-\\dfrac{5}{2},$ we can complete the formula for the $n$th term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot (-2)^{n-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{2}\\cdot (-2)^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can simplify a bit further by manipulating the exponents, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =-\\frac{5}{2}(-2)^{n-1} \\\\  & =5\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2})\\cdot (-2)^{n-1} \\\\  & =5\\cdot (-2)^{-1}\\cdot (-2)^{n-1} \\\\  & =5\\cdot (-2)^{n-2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186078203 :question/problem "Given that the $5$th term of a geometric sequence is $9$, and the common ratio is $3,$ find the second term."] [17592186078203 :question/worked-solution "The common ratio is $r=3,$ so we can start writing the formula for the $n$th term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {r}^{n-1} \\\\  & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {3}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, we still need to figure out the first term $a_1.$ We know that the $5$th term is $a_5=9,$ so we can solve for the first term as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{5} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {3}^{5-1} \\\\ 9 & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {3}^{4} \\\\ 9 & ={a}_{1}\\cdot 81 \\\\ \\frac{9}{81} & ={a}_{1} \\\\ \\frac{1}{9} & ={a}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that we know the first term is $a_1=\\dfrac{1}{9},$ we can complete the formula for the $n$th term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {3}^{n-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\cdot {3}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we can use this formula to compute the second term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{9}\\cdot {3}^{2-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the second term is $a_2 = \\dfrac{1}{3}.$"] ["question-f438fee9-fd2e-5bc4-8ed6-aceb6e4fcc33" :question/id #uuid "f438fee9-fd2e-5bc4-8ed6-aceb6e4fcc33"] ["question-f438fee9-fd2e-5bc4-8ed6-aceb6e4fcc33" :question/math-academy-id "q-265738"] ["question-f438fee9-fd2e-5bc4-8ed6-aceb6e4fcc33" :question/problem "The first term of a geometric sequence is $32,$ and the common ratio is $-\\frac{1}{2}.$  The $12$th term of this sequence is{{field-1}}."] ["question-f438fee9-fd2e-5bc4-8ed6-aceb6e4fcc33" :question/worked-solution "The first term is ${a}_{1}=32,$ and the common ratio is $r=-\\frac{1}{2},$ so we can write the formula for the $n$th term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {r}^{n-1} \\\\  & =32\\cdot {(-\\frac{1}{2})}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the $12$th term, we can use this formula with $n=12:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =32\\cdot {(-\\frac{1}{2})}^{n-1} \\\\ {a}_{12} & =32\\cdot {(-\\frac{1}{2})}^{12-1} \\\\  & =32\\cdot {(-\\frac{1}{2})}^{11} \\\\  & =-{2}^{5}\\cdot \\frac{1}{{2}^{11}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{2}^{6}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{64}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $12$th term is ${a}_{12}=-\\frac{1}{64}.$"] ["question-f438fee9-fd2e-5bc4-8ed6-aceb6e4fcc33" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-26653816-dfb8-59e5-8d87-31577cdbb120" :answer-field/id #uuid "26653816-dfb8-59e5-8d87-31577cdbb120"] ["answer-1dd5ec84-7a08-5f98-8682-c2c50317fdda" :answer/id #uuid "1dd5ec84-7a08-5f98-8682-c2c50317fdda"] ["answer-1dd5ec84-7a08-5f98-8682-c2c50317fdda" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-1dd5ec84-7a08-5f98-8682-c2c50317fdda" :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{64}"] ["answer-field-26653816-dfb8-59e5-8d87-31577cdbb120" :answer-field/key "field-1"] ["answer-field-26653816-dfb8-59e5-8d87-31577cdbb120" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-26653816-dfb8-59e5-8d87-31577cdbb120" :answer-field/correct "answer-1dd5ec84-7a08-5f98-8682-c2c50317fdda"] ["answer-field-26653816-dfb8-59e5-8d87-31577cdbb120" :answer-field/choices "answer-1dd5ec84-7a08-5f98-8682-c2c50317fdda"] ["question-f438fee9-fd2e-5bc4-8ed6-aceb6e4fcc33" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-26653816-dfb8-59e5-8d87-31577cdbb120"] [17592186078558 :knowledge-point/questions "question-f438fee9-fd2e-5bc4-8ed6-aceb6e4fcc33"] ["question-91775cc6-b3ff-5403-8a6d-5a5294e1af4c" :question/id #uuid "91775cc6-b3ff-5403-8a6d-5a5294e1af4c"] ["question-91775cc6-b3ff-5403-8a6d-5a5294e1af4c" :question/math-academy-id "q-265737"] ["question-91775cc6-b3ff-5403-8a6d-5a5294e1af4c" :question/problem "The first term of a geometric sequence is $-\\frac{1}{81},$ and the common ratio is $-3.$ The $9$th term of this sequence is{{field-1}}."] ["question-91775cc6-b3ff-5403-8a6d-5a5294e1af4c" :question/worked-solution "The first term is ${a}_{1}=-\\frac{1}{81},$ and the common ratio is $r=-3,$ so we can write the formula for the $n$th term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {r}^{n-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{81}\\cdot (-3)^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the $9$th term, we can use this formula with $n=9:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =-\\frac{1}{81}\\cdot (-3)^{n-1} \\\\ {a}_{9} & =-\\frac{1}{81}\\cdot (-3)^{9-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{81}\\cdot (-3)^{8} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{3}^{4}}\\cdot {3}^{8} \\\\  & =-{3}^{4} \\\\  & =-81\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $9$th term is ${a}_{9}=-81.$"] ["question-91775cc6-b3ff-5403-8a6d-5a5294e1af4c" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-b77092c7-1268-5f33-a5db-81532ae19c78" :answer-field/id #uuid "b77092c7-1268-5f33-a5db-81532ae19c78"] ["answer-910334bb-a236-530a-b15b-4e9e5b6ad92e" :answer/id #uuid "910334bb-a236-530a-b15b-4e9e5b6ad92e"] ["answer-910334bb-a236-530a-b15b-4e9e5b6ad92e" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-910334bb-a236-530a-b15b-4e9e5b6ad92e" :answer/value "-81"] ["answer-field-b77092c7-1268-5f33-a5db-81532ae19c78" :answer-field/key "field-1"] ["answer-field-b77092c7-1268-5f33-a5db-81532ae19c78" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-b77092c7-1268-5f33-a5db-81532ae19c78" :answer-field/correct "answer-910334bb-a236-530a-b15b-4e9e5b6ad92e"] ["answer-field-b77092c7-1268-5f33-a5db-81532ae19c78" :answer-field/choices "answer-910334bb-a236-530a-b15b-4e9e5b6ad92e"] ["question-91775cc6-b3ff-5403-8a6d-5a5294e1af4c" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-b77092c7-1268-5f33-a5db-81532ae19c78"] [17592186078558 :knowledge-point/questions "question-91775cc6-b3ff-5403-8a6d-5a5294e1af4c"] ["question-1bbae00a-a76f-5b1d-a767-0acf7498bde8" :question/id #uuid "1bbae00a-a76f-5b1d-a767-0acf7498bde8"] ["question-1bbae00a-a76f-5b1d-a767-0acf7498bde8" :question/math-academy-id "q-5449"] ["question-1bbae00a-a76f-5b1d-a767-0acf7498bde8" :question/problem "Find the equation for the $n$th term of a geometric sequence if the $5$th term is $16$ and the common ratio is $\\frac{2}{3}.$"] ["question-1bbae00a-a76f-5b1d-a767-0acf7498bde8" :question/worked-solution "The common ratio is $r=\\frac{2}{3},$ so we can start writing the formula for the $n$th term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {r}^{n-1} \\\\  & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {(\\frac{2}{3})}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, we still need to figure out the first term ${a}_{1}.$ We know that the $5$th term is ${a}_{5}=16,$ so we can solve for the first term as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{5} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {(\\frac{2}{3})}^{5-1} \\\\ 16 & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {(\\frac{2}{3})}^{4} \\\\ {2}^{4} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot (\\frac{{2}^{4}}{{3}^{4}}) \\\\ \\frac{{2}^{4}\\cdot {3}^{4}}{{2}^{4}} & ={a}_{1} \\\\ {3}^{4} & ={a}_{1} \\\\ 81 & ={a}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that we know the first term is ${a}_{1}=81,$ we can complete the formula for the $n$th term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {(\\frac{2}{3})}^{n-1} \\\\  & =81\\cdot {(\\frac{2}{3})}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-1bbae00a-a76f-5b1d-a767-0acf7498bde8" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-93f0a508-6eba-52dd-97c6-cb5ace58658c" :answer-field/id #uuid "93f0a508-6eba-52dd-97c6-cb5ace58658c"] ["answer-0aa368f5-9980-5af5-a908-3b9b819b0121" :answer/id #uuid "0aa368f5-9980-5af5-a908-3b9b819b0121"] ["answer-0aa368f5-9980-5af5-a908-3b9b819b0121" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-0aa368f5-9980-5af5-a908-3b9b819b0121" :answer/value "{a}_{n}=100\\cdot {(\\frac{2}{3})}^{n-1}"] ["answer-a7cb3144-a22f-5f9b-a7a4-6681a52052c2" :answer/id #uuid "a7cb3144-a22f-5f9b-a7a4-6681a52052c2"] ["answer-a7cb3144-a22f-5f9b-a7a4-6681a52052c2" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-a7cb3144-a22f-5f9b-a7a4-6681a52052c2" :answer/value "{a}_{n}=16\\cdot {(\\frac{2}{3})}^{n-1}"] ["answer-a8bc2a3c-15ca-50bd-b78f-91ffcfb5a2d5" :answer/id #uuid "a8bc2a3c-15ca-50bd-b78f-91ffcfb5a2d5"] ["answer-a8bc2a3c-15ca-50bd-b78f-91ffcfb5a2d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-a8bc2a3c-15ca-50bd-b78f-91ffcfb5a2d5" :answer/value "{a}_{n}=49\\cdot {(\\frac{2}{3})}^{n-1}"] ["answer-cc516a3f-e478-5de4-865d-84d26bdbc656" :answer/id #uuid "cc516a3f-e478-5de4-865d-84d26bdbc656"] ["answer-cc516a3f-e478-5de4-865d-84d26bdbc656" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-cc516a3f-e478-5de4-865d-84d26bdbc656" :answer/value "{a}_{n}=64\\cdot {(\\frac{2}{3})}^{n-1}"] ["answer-eca10867-76a4-52f1-be58-955b24419718" :answer/id #uuid "eca10867-76a4-52f1-be58-955b24419718"] ["answer-eca10867-76a4-52f1-be58-955b24419718" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-eca10867-76a4-52f1-be58-955b24419718" :answer/value "{a}_{n}=81\\cdot {(\\frac{2}{3})}^{n-1}"] ["answer-field-93f0a508-6eba-52dd-97c6-cb5ace58658c" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-93f0a508-6eba-52dd-97c6-cb5ace58658c" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-93f0a508-6eba-52dd-97c6-cb5ace58658c" :answer-field/correct "answer-eca10867-76a4-52f1-be58-955b24419718"] ["answer-field-93f0a508-6eba-52dd-97c6-cb5ace58658c" :answer-field/choices "answer-0aa368f5-9980-5af5-a908-3b9b819b0121"] ["answer-field-93f0a508-6eba-52dd-97c6-cb5ace58658c" :answer-field/choices "answer-a7cb3144-a22f-5f9b-a7a4-6681a52052c2"] ["answer-field-93f0a508-6eba-52dd-97c6-cb5ace58658c" :answer-field/choices "answer-a8bc2a3c-15ca-50bd-b78f-91ffcfb5a2d5"] ["answer-field-93f0a508-6eba-52dd-97c6-cb5ace58658c" :answer-field/choices "answer-cc516a3f-e478-5de4-865d-84d26bdbc656"] ["answer-field-93f0a508-6eba-52dd-97c6-cb5ace58658c" :answer-field/choices "answer-eca10867-76a4-52f1-be58-955b24419718"] ["question-1bbae00a-a76f-5b1d-a767-0acf7498bde8" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-93f0a508-6eba-52dd-97c6-cb5ace58658c"] [17592186078559 :knowledge-point/questions "question-1bbae00a-a76f-5b1d-a767-0acf7498bde8"] ["question-18bc1e21-0c4b-52f3-824f-e719cd86e034" :question/id #uuid "18bc1e21-0c4b-52f3-824f-e719cd86e034"] ["question-18bc1e21-0c4b-52f3-824f-e719cd86e034" :question/math-academy-id "q-5450"] ["question-18bc1e21-0c4b-52f3-824f-e719cd86e034" :question/problem "Find the equation for the $n$th term of a geometric sequence if the $6$th term is $-\\frac{1}{5}$ and the common ratio is $-\\frac{1}{5}.$"] ["question-18bc1e21-0c4b-52f3-824f-e719cd86e034" :question/worked-solution "The common ratio is $r=-\\frac{1}{5},$ so we can start writing the formula for the $n$th term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {r}^{n-1} \\\\  & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {(-\\frac{1}{5})}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, we still need to figure out the first term ${a}_{1}.$ We know that the $6$th term is ${a}_{6}=-\\frac{1}{5},$ so we can solve for the first term as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{6} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {(-\\frac{1}{5})}^{6-1} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{5} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {(-\\frac{1}{5})}^{5} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{5} & =-{a}_{1}\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{5})}^{5} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{5} & =-{a}_{1}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{{5}^{5}}) \\\\ {5}^{4} & ={a}_{1} \\\\ 625 & ={a}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that we know the first term is ${a}_{1}=625,$ we can complete the formula for the $n$th term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {(-\\frac{1}{5})}^{n-1} \\\\  & =625\\cdot {(-\\frac{1}{5})}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-18bc1e21-0c4b-52f3-824f-e719cd86e034" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-9d6e6324-1bb7-5c0e-a897-1048511dc113" :answer-field/id #uuid "9d6e6324-1bb7-5c0e-a897-1048511dc113"] ["answer-7d26afe6-a3f8-5d84-83c8-1468c5a521e7" :answer/id #uuid "7d26afe6-a3f8-5d84-83c8-1468c5a521e7"] ["answer-7d26afe6-a3f8-5d84-83c8-1468c5a521e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-7d26afe6-a3f8-5d84-83c8-1468c5a521e7" :answer/value "{a}_{n}=-125\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{5})}^{n-1}"] ["answer-f723a1bb-4bd1-5093-8a09-931299bce976" :answer/id #uuid "f723a1bb-4bd1-5093-8a09-931299bce976"] ["answer-f723a1bb-4bd1-5093-8a09-931299bce976" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-f723a1bb-4bd1-5093-8a09-931299bce976" :answer/value "{a}_{n}=-625\\cdot {(-\\frac{1}{5})}^{n-1}"] ["answer-d08576a1-0a16-5570-9a0f-9b630cd00e74" :answer/id #uuid "d08576a1-0a16-5570-9a0f-9b630cd00e74"] ["answer-d08576a1-0a16-5570-9a0f-9b630cd00e74" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-d08576a1-0a16-5570-9a0f-9b630cd00e74" :answer/value "{a}_{n}=-625\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{5})}^{n}"] ["answer-0b365dcf-dfb8-5ede-acf7-bff7804315f6" :answer/id #uuid "0b365dcf-dfb8-5ede-acf7-bff7804315f6"] ["answer-0b365dcf-dfb8-5ede-acf7-bff7804315f6" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-0b365dcf-dfb8-5ede-acf7-bff7804315f6" :answer/value "{a}_{n}=125\\cdot {(-\\frac{1}{5})}^{n}"] ["answer-838f58f2-22d1-5628-b984-cb6bd81d4f74" :answer/id #uuid "838f58f2-22d1-5628-b984-cb6bd81d4f74"] ["answer-838f58f2-22d1-5628-b984-cb6bd81d4f74" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-838f58f2-22d1-5628-b984-cb6bd81d4f74" :answer/value "{a}_{n}=625\\cdot {(-\\frac{1}{5})}^{n-1}"] ["answer-field-9d6e6324-1bb7-5c0e-a897-1048511dc113" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-9d6e6324-1bb7-5c0e-a897-1048511dc113" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-9d6e6324-1bb7-5c0e-a897-1048511dc113" :answer-field/correct "answer-838f58f2-22d1-5628-b984-cb6bd81d4f74"] ["answer-field-9d6e6324-1bb7-5c0e-a897-1048511dc113" :answer-field/choices "answer-7d26afe6-a3f8-5d84-83c8-1468c5a521e7"] ["answer-field-9d6e6324-1bb7-5c0e-a897-1048511dc113" :answer-field/choices "answer-f723a1bb-4bd1-5093-8a09-931299bce976"] ["answer-field-9d6e6324-1bb7-5c0e-a897-1048511dc113" :answer-field/choices "answer-d08576a1-0a16-5570-9a0f-9b630cd00e74"] ["answer-field-9d6e6324-1bb7-5c0e-a897-1048511dc113" :answer-field/choices "answer-0b365dcf-dfb8-5ede-acf7-bff7804315f6"] ["answer-field-9d6e6324-1bb7-5c0e-a897-1048511dc113" :answer-field/choices "answer-838f58f2-22d1-5628-b984-cb6bd81d4f74"] ["question-18bc1e21-0c4b-52f3-824f-e719cd86e034" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-9d6e6324-1bb7-5c0e-a897-1048511dc113"] [17592186078559 :knowledge-point/questions "question-18bc1e21-0c4b-52f3-824f-e719cd86e034"] ["question-cb4d13f6-05f0-58f1-8216-e5e0e82521cb" :question/id #uuid "cb4d13f6-05f0-58f1-8216-e5e0e82521cb"] ["question-cb4d13f6-05f0-58f1-8216-e5e0e82521cb" :question/math-academy-id "q-265843"] ["question-cb4d13f6-05f0-58f1-8216-e5e0e82521cb" :question/problem "If the sixth term of a geometric sequence is $\\frac{1}{16}$ and the common ratio is $\\frac{1}{4},$ then the third term of this sequence is{{field-1}}."] ["question-cb4d13f6-05f0-58f1-8216-e5e0e82521cb" :question/worked-solution "The common ratio is $r=\\frac{1}{4},$ so we can start writing the formula for the $n$th term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {r}^{n-1} \\\\  & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{4})}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, we still need to figure out the first term ${a}_{1}.$ We know that the $6$th term is ${a}_{6}=16,$ so we can solve for the first term as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{6} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{4})}^{6-1} \\\\ \\frac{1}{16} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{4})}^{5} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{4}^{2}} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot \\frac{1}{{4}^{5}} \\\\ \\frac{{4}^{5}}{{4}^{2}} & ={a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =64\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that we know the first term is ${a}_{1}=64,$ we can complete the formula for the $n$th term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{4})}^{n-1} \\\\  & =64\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{4})}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we can use this formula to compute the third term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{3} & =64\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{4})}^{3-1} \\\\  & ={4}^{3}\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{4})}^{2} \\\\  & ={4}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{{4}^{2}} \\\\  & ={4}^{1} \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the third term  is ${a}_{3}=4.$"] ["question-cb4d13f6-05f0-58f1-8216-e5e0e82521cb" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-821f6ff9-8b02-5321-9f6c-8231f646103b" :answer-field/id #uuid "821f6ff9-8b02-5321-9f6c-8231f646103b"] ["answer-f7fc47b7-94cb-597e-9fb8-34e73e5166b1" :answer/id #uuid "f7fc47b7-94cb-597e-9fb8-34e73e5166b1"] ["answer-f7fc47b7-94cb-597e-9fb8-34e73e5166b1" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-f7fc47b7-94cb-597e-9fb8-34e73e5166b1" :answer/value "4"] ["answer-field-821f6ff9-8b02-5321-9f6c-8231f646103b" :answer-field/key "field-1"] ["answer-field-821f6ff9-8b02-5321-9f6c-8231f646103b" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-821f6ff9-8b02-5321-9f6c-8231f646103b" :answer-field/correct "answer-f7fc47b7-94cb-597e-9fb8-34e73e5166b1"] ["answer-field-821f6ff9-8b02-5321-9f6c-8231f646103b" :answer-field/choices "answer-f7fc47b7-94cb-597e-9fb8-34e73e5166b1"] ["question-cb4d13f6-05f0-58f1-8216-e5e0e82521cb" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-821f6ff9-8b02-5321-9f6c-8231f646103b"] [17592186078560 :knowledge-point/questions "question-cb4d13f6-05f0-58f1-8216-e5e0e82521cb"] ["question-b5f78cff-3c2d-5ff5-b715-c8fb25e53460" :question/id #uuid "b5f78cff-3c2d-5ff5-b715-c8fb25e53460"] ["question-b5f78cff-3c2d-5ff5-b715-c8fb25e53460" :question/math-academy-id "q-109828"] ["question-b5f78cff-3c2d-5ff5-b715-c8fb25e53460" :question/problem "Given that the $5$th term of a geometric sequence is $-125$, and the common ratio is $5,$ find the formula for the $n$th term."] ["question-b5f78cff-3c2d-5ff5-b715-c8fb25e53460" :question/worked-solution "The common ratio is $r=5,$ so we can start writing the formula for the $n$th term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {r}^{n-1} \\\\  & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {5}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, we still need to figure out the first term ${a}_{1}.$ We know that the $5$th term is ${a}_{5}=-125,$ so we can solve for the first term as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{5} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {5}^{5-1} \\\\ -125 & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {5}^{4} \\\\ -{5}^{3} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {5}^{4} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{5} & ={a}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that we know the first term is ${a}_{1}=-\\frac{1}{5},$ we can complete the formula for the $n$th term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {5}^{n-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot {5}^{n-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{{5}^{n-1}}{5} \\\\  & =-{5}^{n-2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-b5f78cff-3c2d-5ff5-b715-c8fb25e53460" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] ["answer-field-0d82d16e-44b2-54a6-8e45-2ab848923d07" :answer-field/id #uuid "0d82d16e-44b2-54a6-8e45-2ab848923d07"] ["answer-1d9acfbd-b37d-5bf8-8563-021375b3f0ac" :answer/id #uuid "1d9acfbd-b37d-5bf8-8563-021375b3f0ac"] ["answer-1d9acfbd-b37d-5bf8-8563-021375b3f0ac" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-1d9acfbd-b37d-5bf8-8563-021375b3f0ac" :answer/value "{a}_{n}=-(-5)^{n-2}"] ["answer-71563d96-72fd-5a7a-873a-b97ad8340ba8" :answer/id #uuid "71563d96-72fd-5a7a-873a-b97ad8340ba8"] ["answer-71563d96-72fd-5a7a-873a-b97ad8340ba8" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-71563d96-72fd-5a7a-873a-b97ad8340ba8" :answer/value "{a}_{n}=-{(\\frac{1}{5})}^{n-2}"] ["answer-eec28517-10af-546d-b87d-a5fb95584b92" :answer/id #uuid "eec28517-10af-546d-b87d-a5fb95584b92"] ["answer-eec28517-10af-546d-b87d-a5fb95584b92" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-eec28517-10af-546d-b87d-a5fb95584b92" :answer/value "{a}_{n}=-{(\\frac{1}{5})}^{n}"] ["answer-0a702943-5d20-5d78-b4eb-5b9620b8469b" :answer/id #uuid "0a702943-5d20-5d78-b4eb-5b9620b8469b"] ["answer-0a702943-5d20-5d78-b4eb-5b9620b8469b" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-0a702943-5d20-5d78-b4eb-5b9620b8469b" :answer/value "{a}_{n}=-{5}^{n-1}"] ["answer-fce13607-7057-5951-b22c-0a53487566f8" :answer/id #uuid "fce13607-7057-5951-b22c-0a53487566f8"] ["answer-fce13607-7057-5951-b22c-0a53487566f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-fce13607-7057-5951-b22c-0a53487566f8" :answer/value "{a}_{n}=-{5}^{n-2}"] ["answer-field-0d82d16e-44b2-54a6-8e45-2ab848923d07" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-0d82d16e-44b2-54a6-8e45-2ab848923d07" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-0d82d16e-44b2-54a6-8e45-2ab848923d07" :answer-field/correct "answer-fce13607-7057-5951-b22c-0a53487566f8"] ["answer-field-0d82d16e-44b2-54a6-8e45-2ab848923d07" :answer-field/choices "answer-1d9acfbd-b37d-5bf8-8563-021375b3f0ac"] ["answer-field-0d82d16e-44b2-54a6-8e45-2ab848923d07" :answer-field/choices "answer-71563d96-72fd-5a7a-873a-b97ad8340ba8"] ["answer-field-0d82d16e-44b2-54a6-8e45-2ab848923d07" :answer-field/choices "answer-eec28517-10af-546d-b87d-a5fb95584b92"] ["answer-field-0d82d16e-44b2-54a6-8e45-2ab848923d07" :answer-field/choices "answer-0a702943-5d20-5d78-b4eb-5b9620b8469b"] ["answer-field-0d82d16e-44b2-54a6-8e45-2ab848923d07" :answer-field/choices "answer-fce13607-7057-5951-b22c-0a53487566f8"] ["question-b5f78cff-3c2d-5ff5-b715-c8fb25e53460" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-0d82d16e-44b2-54a6-8e45-2ab848923d07"] [17592186078560 :knowledge-point/questions "question-b5f78cff-3c2d-5ff5-b715-c8fb25e53460"] [17592186079626 :tutorial/content "The general formula for the $n$th term of a geometric sequence is \n\n$$\na_n = a_1 \\cdot r^{n-1},\n$$\n\nwhere $a_1$ is the first term and $r$ is the common ratio.\n\nTo illustrate how this works, suppose we want to find the $10$th term of the following geometric sequence:\n\n$$\n3, \\: 6, \\: 12, \\: \\ldots\n$$\n\nThe first term is $a_1=3,$ and the common ratio is $r=2,$ so we can write the formula for the $n$th term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {r}^{n-1} \\\\  & =3\\cdot {2}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the $10$th term, we can use this formula with $n={\\color{blue}10}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =3\\cdot {2}^{n-1} \\\\ {a}_{10} & =3\\cdot {2}^{10-1} \\\\  & =3\\cdot {2}^{9} \\\\  & =3\\cdot 512 \\\\  & =1\\,536\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $10$th term is $a_{10}=1\\,536.$ Using the formula was much quicker than writing out all $10$ terms of the sequence!"] [17592186078695 :activity/expected-seconds 600.0]] "retractions" [[17592186078202 :question/problem "The first term of a geometric sequence is $2$, and the common ratio is $3$. What is the $9$th term?"] [17592186078202 :question/worked-solution "The first term is $a_1=2$, and the common ratio is $r=3$, so we can write the formula for the $n$th term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na_{n} &= a_{1} \\cdot r^{n - 1} \\\\\n&= 2 \\cdot 3^{n - 1}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the $9$th term, we can use this formula with\n\n$$\nn={\\color{blue}9}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na_{n} &= 2 \\cdot 3^{n - 1} \\\\\na_{9} &= 2 \\cdot 3^{9 - 1} \\\\\n&= 2 \\cdot 3^{8} \\\\\n&= 2 \\cdot 6561 \\\\\n&= 13122\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $9$th term is\n\n$$\na_{9}=13\\,122\n$$"] [17592186078204 :question/problem "Find the formula for the $n$th term of a sequence if the $6$th term is $80$ and the common ratio is $-2$."] [17592186078204 :question/worked-solution "The common ratio is $r=-2$, so we can start writing the formula for the $n$th term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na_{n} &= a_{1} \\cdot r^{n - 1} \\\\\n&= a_{1} \\cdot (-2)^{n - 1}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, we still need to figure out the first term $a_1$. We know that the $6$th term is $a_6=80$, so we can solve for the first term as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na_{6} &= a_{1} \\cdot (-2)^{6 - 1} \\\\\n80 &= a_{1} \\cdot (-2)^{5} \\\\\n80 &= a_{1} \\cdot (-32) \\\\\n- \\frac{80}{32} &= a_{1} \\\\\n- \\frac{5}{2} &= a_{1}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that we know the first term is\n\n$$\na_1=-\\dfrac{5}{2}\n$$\n\nwe can complete the formula for the $n$th term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na_{n} &= a_{1} \\cdot (-2)^{n - 1} \\\\\n&=-\\frac{5}{2} \\cdot (-2)^{n - 1}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can simplify a bit further by manipulating the exponents, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na_{n} &= -\\frac{5}{2}(-2)^{n - 1} \\\\\n&= 5 \\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2}) \\cdot (-2)^{n - 1} \\\\\n&= 5 \\cdot (-2)^{-1} \\cdot (-2)^{n - 1} \\\\\n&= 5 \\cdot (-2)^{n - 2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186078203 :question/problem "Given that the $5$th term of a geometric sequence is $9$, and the common ratio is $3$, find the second term."] [17592186078203 :question/worked-solution "The common ratio is $r=3$, so we can start writing the formula for the $n$th term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na_{n} &= a_{1} \\cdot r^{n - 1} \\\\\n&= a_{1} \\cdot 3^{n - 1}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, we still need to figure out the first term $a_1$. We know that the $5$th term is $a_5=9$, so we can solve for the first term as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na_{5} &= a_{1} \\cdot 3^{5 - 1} \\\\\n9 &= a_{1} \\cdot 3^{4} \\\\\n9 &= a_{1} \\cdot 81 \\\\\n\\frac{9}{81} &= a_{1} \\\\\n\\frac{1}{9} &= a_{1}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that we know the first term is\n\n$$\na_1=\\dfrac{1}{9}\n$$\n\nwe can complete the formula for the $n$th term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na_{n} &= a_{1} \\cdot 3^{n - 1} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{9} \\cdot 3^{n - 1}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we can use this formula to compute the second term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na_{2} &= \\frac{1}{9} \\cdot 3^{2 - 1} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{9} \\cdot 3 \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the second term is\n\n$$\na_2 = \\dfrac{1}{3}\n$$"] [17592186079626 :tutorial/content "The general formula for the $n$th term of a geometric sequence is\n\n$$\na_n = a_1 \\cdot r^{n-1}\n$$\n\nwhere $a_1$ is the first term and $r$ is the common ratio.\n\nTo illustrate how this works, suppose we want to find the $10$th term of the following geometric sequence:\n\n$$\n3, \\: 6, \\: 12, \\: \\ldots\n$$\n\nThe first term is $a_1=3$, and the common ratio is $r=2$, so we can write the formula for the $n$th term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na_{n} &= a_{1} \\cdot r^{n - 1} \\\\\n&= 3 \\cdot 2^{n - 1}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the $10$th term, we can use this formula with\n\n$$\nn={\\color{blue}10}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na_{n} &= 3 \\cdot 2^{n - 1} \\\\\na_{10} &= 3 \\cdot 2^{10 - 1} \\\\\n&= 3 \\cdot 2^{9} \\\\\n&= 3 \\cdot 512 \\\\\n&= 1536\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $10$th term is\n\n$$\na_{10}=1\\,536\n$$\n\nUsing the formula was much quicker than writing out all $10$ terms of the sequence!"]]}]